<title>GERMANY: Statement issued by G7 nations in Berlin.</title>
<headline>Statement issued by G7 nations in Berlin.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-02-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a transcript of the statement issued by the G7 nations in Berlin. The text was presented by the U.S. delegation in English.</p>
<p>&quot;We discussed the developments on currency and financial markets.</p>
<p>We believe that major misalignments in exchange markets, noted in our April 1995 communique, have been corrected.</p>
<p>We reaffirmed our views that exchange rates should reflect economic fundamentals and that excess volatility is undesirable.</p>
<p>We agreed to monitor developments on the currency markets and to coooperate as appropriate.&quot;</p>
<p>The U.S. Germany, Japan, France, Italy, Canada and Britain are members of the G7.</p>
<p>--Berlin Newsroom, +49 30 2039810</p>
</text>
